{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1204862-question-about-predatory-aura","id":1204862,"title":"Question about predatory aura","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-09T07:49:01-07:00","id":1204862,"title":"Question about predatory aura","content":"Hey,<br /> <br /> In 1st edition, a vampire could tell how old another vampire is, even could compare two nearby vampires which one is older. In the 2nd edition, it is ambiguous, nothing is mentioned about this ability, only that you can feel another vampire. Is this ability was taken away in the 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1036-altern","name":"Altern","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T08:50:02-07:00","id":1204876,"title":"","content":"Correct, you normally cannot tell the age of a vampire from Predatory Aura. That said, I *think* (Don't quote me) that Half-Damned for the Dhampir or Revenants has some kind of sense where they can tell if someone is a vampire, their clan, and so forth - I don't know if age or blood potency is one of those elements. I am away from my books right now, but I can look later if it's important to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T08:52:29-07:00","id":1204877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altern</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1204862-question-about-predatory-aura#post1204862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey,<br /> <br /> In 1st edition, a vampire could tell how old another vampire is, even could compare two nearby vampires which one is older. In the 2nd edition, it is ambiguous, nothing is mentioned about this ability, only that you can feel another vampire. Is this ability was taken away in the 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1st Edition vampires could not really tell each other\u2019s ages, but could tell relative Blood Potency thanks to the Predator\u2019s Taint. The weaker vampire wanted to run, the stronger vampire wanted to chase, and both had to fight to suppress that instinct. The equivalent in 2nd Edition is the Predatory Aura, which is lashed out with voluntarily, and includes an element of Blood Potency, but also an element of Power Attributes, and an element of luck.<br /> <br /> So in 1e, when you met another vampire for the first time, you could tell if their blood was stronger or weaker than yours based on your instinctive reaction to them. In 2e, one of you would have to choose to Lash Out, and you would only be able to tell that the loser of the clash was overall less forceful in that moment, maybe because of thinner blood, maybe because of weaker personality, maybe because it was just an off day for them. Most likely some combination of the three You\u2019d have to regularly clash with someone to tell who was winning the most consistently to know who had the stronger beast, and still it might not be all about Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s going by a literal interpretation of the rules, of course. Personally, I always liked the idea that vampires, in a vague sense, can tell other vampire\u2019s Blood Potency relative to their own. And I like the idea of the instinct to run from stronger vampires or chase weaker ones. So, in my games, that still happens, it just isn\u2019t mechanically enforced, and the instinct isn\u2019t strong enough to force a Frenzy check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-09-2018, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T10:22:16-07:00","id":1204899,"title":"","content":"Furthermore, if I'm not wrong, since torpor lower the bp, in first edition you could be in front of an ancient just awake from torpor and have a greater BP (not meaning you are older).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T17:08:27-07:00","id":1205017,"title":"","content":"That is correct. Nothing innately lets vampires in either edition detect another vampires approximate age, just their approximate personal power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T08:10:38-07:00","id":1205216,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there ways to do so by tasting their blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:57:05-07:00","id":1205266,"title":"","content":"Maybe on an exceptional success on a Taste of Blood roll might let you discern age if your ST is kind enough. Depends on how and what you gain from &quot;You can discern extensive<br /> details from the blood.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T10:15:46-07:00","id":1205273,"title":"","content":"wondered for a bit... does a revenant get Predatory Aura, if so its probaly quite a boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T10:36:21-07:00","id":1205286,"title":"","content":"Yeah they get an aura. Nothing in their rules says otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T19:19:40-07:00","id":1208283,"title":"","content":"You should be able to use Auspex to get an approximation in regard to 2nd Edition, though.<br /> <br /> Question(s) you could possibly ask with its first dot:<br /> <br /> <i>Who here has a higher blood potency than me?<br /> <br /> Who here has the highest blood potency?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T00:10:49-07:00","id":1208349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1204862-question-about-predatory-aura?p=1208283#post1208283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should be able to use Auspex to get an approximation in regard to 2nd Edition, though.<br /> <br /> Question(s) you could possibly ask with its first dot:<br /> <br /> <i>Who here has a higher blood potency than me?<br /> <br /> Who here has the highest blood potency?</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure about it. The first power is literally focused on immediate dangers and weakness. Asking who has the highest BP seems to me off theme and a little forced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-18-2018, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T01:54:08-07:00","id":1208365,"title":"","content":"It's certainly a borderline application of Auspex. Even if you allowed such questions, you're giving vague responses. I would certainly exercise a bit of ST discretion to not allow that precise question over a more general idea of vampric power, so things like higher current blood pools, breadth and depth of Disciplines/other powers, and Blood Potency could all influence the response..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T02:39:37-07:00","id":1208376,"title":"","content":"I'd personally just allow the question: Who here has the lowest BP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T06:10:05-07:00","id":1208411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1204862-question-about-predatory-aura?p=1208283#post1208283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should be able to use Auspex to get an approximation in regard to 2nd Edition, though.<br /> <br /> Question(s) you could possibly ask with its first dot:<br /> <br /> <i>Who here has a higher blood potency than me?<br /> <br /> Who here has the highest blood potency?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think better questions would be:<br /> <br /> Who is the most dangerous right now?<br /> Who has the greatest weakness?<br /> <br /> ( remember the first dot is about immediate danger and weakness )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1204862-question-about-predatory-aura?p=1208376#post1208376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd personally just allow the question: Who here has the lowest BP.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we are still talking the first dot, That doesn't show weakness or immediate danger.<br /> An Elder vampire could have woken from centuries of sleep and have 1-2 BP and still have the ability to completely obliterate a neonate with the same 1-2 BP. It doesn't mean they are weak or a danger to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-18-2018, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T06:40:41-07:00","id":1208424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1204862-question-about-predatory-aura?p=1208411#post1208411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think better questions would be:<br /> <br /> Who is the most dangerous right now?<br /> Who has the greatest weakness?<br /> <br /> ( remember the first dot is about immediate danger and weakness )<br /> <br /> <br /> If we are still talking the first dot, That doesn't show weakness or immediate danger.<br /> An Elder vampire could have woken from centuries of sleep and have 1-2 BP and still have the ability to completely obliterate a neonate with the same 1-2 BP. It doesn't mean they are weak or a danger to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree. I 'm not very fine with this question in fact but, since the topic was about BP, if you really want to ask for it I would go in this way since it's more about showing a weakness. <br /> By the way, even if it is an elder with all the discipline at 5, still having the lowest bp in the place is a weakness factor. At least it means you cannot activate every discipline you like. But again, it's a borderline question and Auspex is actually particularly inclined to be object of different interpretations and doubts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T07:21:12-07:00","id":1213049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1204862-question-about-predatory-aura?p=1208349#post1208349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not sure about it. The first power is literally focused on immediate dangers and weakness. Asking who has the highest BP seems to me off theme and a little forced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a couple example questions in the book, though.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Who here is the most likely to give me what I want?</b> Blood throbbing through the victim\u2019s jugular vein. The sound of jingling coins from the victim\u2019s pocket.</i><br /> <br /> In the above, whatever constitutes a 'weakness' or 'immediate danger' is a bit flexible. Read the answers. Blood. Money. You aren't sensing danger or weakness in the literal sense in these cases, are you?<br /> <br /> <i><b>Is a vampire here using Auspex 5?</b> A pall of grey smoke hanging in the air. A feeling like someone walked over the vampire\u2019s grave.</i><br /> <br /> And in the above, asking something as forced as 'who has a higher BP' is no more forced than asking if Auspex 5 is being used IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T07:53:24-07:00","id":1213054,"title":"","content":"The first does read as finding a weak point to apply pressure to get what you want, though I could see how someone would consider it a stretch.<br /> <br /> The second is very clearly a potential danger.<br /> <br /> Of course, asking who has the most potent blood is also finding potential threats, so I'd certainly allow it. I just wouldn't allow Auspex to tell you exactly how potent. &quot;Bob the Elder over there has the most potent blood&quot; would be fine, but &quot;Bob the Elder over there has BP 5&quot; is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:04:51-07:00","id":1213056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1204862-question-about-predatory-aura?p=1213049#post1213049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a couple example questions in the book, though.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Who here is the most likely to give me what I want?</b> Blood throbbing through the victim\u2019s jugular vein. The sound of jingling coins from the victim\u2019s pocket.</i><br /> <br /> In the above, whatever constitutes a 'weakness' or 'immediate danger' is a bit flexible. Read the answers. Blood. Money. You aren't sensing danger or weakness in the literal sense in these cases, are you?<br /> <br /> <i><b>Is a vampire here using Auspex 5?</b> A pall of grey smoke hanging in the air. A feeling like someone walked over the vampire\u2019s grave.</i><br /> <br /> And in the above, asking something as forced as 'who has a higher BP' is no more forced than asking if Auspex 5 is being used IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Maina about the two sample questions.<br /> About the first one, in the specific, auspex is providing you the weakness to use in order to obtain what you asked for: &quot;The sound of jingling coins from the victim\u2019s pocket.&quot; Meaning that is corruptible with money.<br /> <br /> The second is clearly a potential danger like someone being obfuscated.<br /> <br /> I'm not completely contrary asking who has the highest BP but I feel it a little out of topic and borderline. But it's a personal feeling more than a belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-29-2018, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:48:52-07:00","id":1213074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1204862-question-about-predatory-aura?p=1213054#post1213054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first does read as finding a weak point to apply pressure to get what you want, though I could see how someone would consider it a stretch.<br /> <br /> The second is very clearly a potential danger.<br /> <br /> Of course, asking who has the most potent blood is also finding potential threats, so I'd certainly allow it.<b> I just wouldn't allow Auspex to tell you exactly how potent.</b> &quot;Bob the Elder over there has the most potent blood&quot; would be fine, but &quot;Bob the Elder over there has BP 5&quot; is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.<br /> <br /> In the same way as the example questions are answered, it should invoke some basic, fun imagery - not a direct answer.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Who here has the highest BP?</b> The smell of blood is headiest around Count Dracula.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T12:54:09-07:00","id":1213154,"title":"","content":"I'd also chalk the specific phrasing of the Auspex 5 question to early installment weirdness. The question should really be, &quot;Is anyone observing us from Twilight?&quot; which is danger, a more sensible question to ask rather than a rating on a sheet, and frankly more useful since it applies to more than just vampires using a specific power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}